RECURSIVE SERENDIPITY

Nesting Cluck / Lucky Brood

Pantheon should distinguish between:

\text{chance event}

and:

\text{a system becoming better at harvesting chance}.

A useful accident can do more than produce one useful result.

It can produce a new:

* detector,
* handle,
* representation,
* operator,
* heuristic,
* route,
* question,
* search policy,
* or capability.

That new machinery can then increase the chance that later useful accidents are noticed, captured, interpreted, and reused.

This is:

\boxed{\textbf{Recursive Serendipity}}

Pantheon handles:

\boxed{\textbf{Nesting Cluck}}

and:

\boxed{\textbf{Lucky Brood}}

⸻

1. Core Pattern

Let:

L_t

be a useful unexpected event at time t.

Pantheon does not stop at:

L_t \rightarrow \text{benefit}.

Instead:

L_t
\rightarrow
\text{notice}
\rightarrow
\text{capture}
\rightarrow
\text{extract}
\rightarrow
\text{reuse}
\rightarrow
\text{larger detection surface}.

Then:

\boxed{
L_t
\rightarrow
M_t
\rightarrow
H_{t+1}
\rightarrow
L_{t+1}
}

where:

* M_t = mechanism extracted from the lucky event,
* H_t = current serendipity harvest surface.

