6. Compounding

If each successful cycle increases harvest capacity:

H_{t+1}>H_t

then later useful accidents become easier to detect.

Conceptually:

P(\text{detect useful }L_{t+1}\mid H_{t+1})
>
P(\text{detect useful }L_{t+1}\mid H_t).

The compounding is therefore not:

\text{luck causes more supernatural luck}.

It is:

\boxed{
\text{captured serendipity creates better machinery for harvesting future serendipity}.
}

